The changed hunk (lines 788-804) is a defensive guard that rejects cyclic reparenting (a plugin moved under itself or its own descendants). This is a denial-of-service / data-integrity hardening, not an authorization change. It does not add, remove, or alter any authentication/role/ownership check, and it does not newly expose any object fetch. The pre-existing lack of a `has_change_plugin_permission` check in `move_plugin` is unchanged code and therefore out of scope. No authorization flaw is introduced by this section.

